-- MEASURED 2026-09-07, both halves, in the corpus world:
--   * the ten kinds are real and present — `tstype_annotation` 53 nodes,
--     `tsnumber_keyword` 44 — and what each MEANS at the four declared layers is
--     a fact about the language, not about prototypes. Forty cells, all
--     `ignored`, closed here.
--   * the prototype question has ZERO SITES. Of 167 unresolved call sites, 152
--     are a bare identifier (an IMPORT — w_cg_module_boundary's residue) and
--     only 13 are member calls; of those, NONE has a literal receiver, so there
--     is no `"s".toUpperCase()` and no `[1,2].at(-1)` anywhere in the corpus.
--     Building it now would be a capability nothing exercises, which this
--     repository forbids by name.
-- A NODE IN TYPE POSITION AND THE TYPE OF A VALUE SHARE A WORD AND NOTHING ELSE.
work(w_type_surface, "DONE 2026-09-07: the ten TypeScript type-node kinds are declared and answered at all four layers; the prototype question was a different item and is w_prototype_of_a_value").
