-- 32. EFFECTS, AND THE TAXONOMY IS NOT OURS TO INVENT. The owner asked whether
-- a standard one exists. It does, and in two versions that disagree usefully -
-- see f_the_effect_taxonomy_already_exists_and_it_is_a_lattice. The one to take
-- is Koka's basic set, because it is closed, named and ORDERED: `total`, `exn`,
-- `div`, `ndet`, `alloc`, `read`, `write`, `io`, with `pure = <div, exn>` and
-- `io = <st, div, exn, ndet>`. An order with a bottom and a top is the thing a
-- model can use; a flat list of labels is not.
--
-- IT IS BLOCKED ON THREE OF ITS OWN MEMBERS and that is why the dependency
-- rows are worth writing down: `exn` is item 28, `read`/`write` are item 30,
-- and `ndet` plus `io` are item 17 - which is to say the effect layer is not a
-- new question at all, it is the JOIN of four questions already queued.
work(w_effect_layer, "the effect axis over Koka's basic set: total, exn, div, ndet, read, write, io").
work_order(w_effect_layer, 32).
